+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two versions of a JSON document rather than the whole new version. The library can apply an RFC 6902 patch but cannot produce one.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `createPatch(from, to)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returning an RFC 6902 JSON Patch that turns `from` into `to` when applied with `applyPatch`.
+- The patch is minimal in scope: it touches only the places that differ, recursing into objects and arrays instead of replacing whole containers.
+- Array insertions and removals yield a single `add` / `remove` for the item; moves yield `move` (or `remove` + `add`); neighbouring items are not rewritten.
+- Neither input is mutated, and the patch shares no object or array with the inputs.
+- Document the function in `README.md`.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-patch-creation`: computing a minimal RFC 6902 patch between two JSON documents.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New module `src/diff.ts` and tests; one new export in `src/index.ts`; README section.
+- No change to `applyPatch` or other existing behaviour; no new dependencies.
